{
 "summary": "Adds manual pruning and block-storage flushing functions to the libbitcoinkernel C API, allowing kernel consumers to open pruned datadirs and prune block storage up to a target height. Refactors prune calculation and file-deletion bookkeeping into BlockManager so block storage operations can execute independently of chainstate flushes, and ensures blocks above the fork point between the last flushed block and the active chain are preserved for reorg recovery.",
 "problem": "Applications using libbitcoinkernel cannot open datadirs created by pruned Bitcoin Core nodes and have no mechanism to prune blocks. Block storage writes and prune tracking were also tightly coupled to FlushStateToDisk in validation.",
 "evidence": [
  "Part of #35627: 'kernel: can't work with pruned blocksdir'",
  "kernel-node/kernel-node#111",
  "Author's description: 'The kernel can't open a data directory that a pruned node created, and it has no way to prune.'"
 ],
 "dependencies": {
  "depends_on": [
   "#36738",
   "#36854"
  ],
