   "#36857"
  ]
 },
 "scope_notes": "Stacked on top of #36738 and #36854; includes multiple internal refactors moving prune locks, limits, and file deletion out of FlushStateToDisk and into BlockManager before exposing the C API surface.",
 "changed_since_previous": "",
 "card": "Adds manual pruning and chainstate flushing functions to the libbitcoinkernel C API (btck_block_manager_prune_up_to_height and btck_chainstate_manager_flush) and enables kernel consumers to open pruned datadirs. Currently, external applications embedding the kernel cannot operate on pruned datadirs or trigger pruning on their own (issue #35627). The underlying block-file deletion logic and prune bookkeeping are extracted from validation's FlushStateToDisk into BlockManager, while ensuring blocks needed for crash recovery during reorgs are retained. This PR is based on #36738 and #36854.",
